        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most people with $300 to spend, the <strong class="text-white">UREVO SpaceWalk 3S</strong>
            is the machine to buy: a powered incline on a 42.5-inch belt for about $250. If you want
            to jog now and then with a bar to hold, the <strong class="text-white">UREVO Strol
            2E</strong> does it for less, and if you simply want the cheapest pad we could verify,
            the <strong class="text-white">UREVO SpaceWalk E1L</strong> is it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Be clear about what this budget buys. It is a good walking machine, not a running
            treadmill, and it is built around a one-year warranty. If running is the goal, the
